atherClient.get` now retries when the server returns 503, making 3 attempts in total. I tested it against a local HTTP server and it behaved as intended in all four cases I tried.\n\n**What changed in `weather.py`:**\n- A 503 response is retried, waiting `backoff * 2**attempt` between tries. With the default `backoff=0.5`, the waits are 0.5s and then 1s.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, the original `HTTPError` is raised as before.\n- Any other HTTP error, and any non-HTTP error such as a timeout or connection failure, is raised straight away with no retry.\n- New `backoff` constructor parameter (default `0.5`), so tests can make the waits short. The attempt count is the class attribute `max_attempts = 3`.\n\n**Test results** (local server, `backoff=0.01`):\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 straight away | data returned | 1 |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | data returned | 3 |\n| 503 every time | `HTTPError 503` raised | 3 |\n| 500 | `HTTPError 500` raised | 1 |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add a test file.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 0, "requests_cache_write": 178619, "requests_cost_usd": 0.926443, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1665, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial10", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 78, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:48:22.829816+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 20.374, "t_checker_s": 2.44, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", 